<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39976" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quam-dĭu</span></b> , less freq. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quandĭu</span></b>  (mostly as two words, sometimes
		separated: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quam voluit diu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Q. Fr. 1, 1, 7</span></i>
			), adv.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Interrog.</i>, <i>how long ago? how
				long?</i> quamdiu id factum est? <i><span class="en">Plaut. Capt.
				5, 3, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quandiu apud vos ero,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Marc. 9, 18</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Rel.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Of time, <i>as long as</i>, <i>until</i>, <i>during</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quamdiu potuit, tacuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. G. 1, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">disces, quamdiu voles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 1, 1, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 12, 52, 13</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<i>Until</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jubebat, ut semper id comesset, quamdiu tamen
					melius invenisset,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lampr. Elag. 29, 7</span></i>
			.— <i>Comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quamdiutius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Not. Tir. p. 35</span></i>
			.—<i>Sup.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">‡ quamdiutissime,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Not. Tir. p. 35</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Of
			inference, <i>inasmuch as</i>, <i>in
			that</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quandiu fecistis uni ex his fratribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Matt. 25, 40</span></i>
			.</div>
